{
 "meta": {"level": "A1", "section": "Grammar", "number": 8, "total_in_level": 9,
  "title": "Adjectives",
  "subtitle": "When an adjective gets -e, the spelling changes, and the basics of comparison",
  "footer": "Language Learning · A1 · Grammar · Adjectives",
  "next": "Next: A1 · pdf 9 — Vocabulary and phrases"},
 "blocks": [
  {"type": "callout", "kind": "tip", "title": "After this PDF you can", "bullets": [
   "decide when an adjective gets <b>-e</b>: <i>een groot huis, het grote huis</i>",
   "spell the adjective with -e (<i>dik → dikke, lief → lieve</i>)",
   "compare with <b>-er ... dan</b> and <b>het -st</b>",
   "use the most common adjectives"]},
  {"type": "h1", "text": "1. -e or no -e?"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "After the verb (<i>Het huis is groot</i>) an adjective never changes. Before a noun it usually gets <b>-e</b>: <i>de grote stad, de grote huizen</i>. There is one exception: <b>no -e</b> with a <b>het-word</b> in the singular after <b>een</b>, <b>geen</b> or no article at all."},
  {"type": "table", "style": "plain", "widths": [4.6, 6.2, 6.2], "head": ["", "de-word", "het-word"], "rows": [
   ["after de / het / deze / dit / mijn", "de grote stad", "het grote huis"],
   ["after een / geen", "een grote stad", "een groot huis"],
   ["no article", "grote steden", "lekker brood"],
   ["plural (always -e)", "de grote steden", "de grote huizen"],
   ["after the verb (never -e)", "De stad is groot.", "Het huis is groot."]]},
  {"type": "callout", "kind": "note", "title": "Only one box has no -e", "text": "Remember the exception, not the rule: <b>een + het-word</b> (and a het-word without any article) → no -e: <i>een <b>klein</b> kind, een <b>mooi</b> huis, <b>koud</b> water</i>. Everywhere else before a noun: -e. English adjectives never change, so this takes practice: say the phrases aloud."},
  {"type": "h1", "text": "2. The spelling with -e"},
  {"type": "table", "style": "plain", "widths": [5.4, 5.2, 6.4], "head": ["Rule", "Example", "More examples"], "rows": [
   ["long vowel: one letter", "groot → grote", "laag → lage, duur → dure"],
   ["short vowel: double consonant", "dik → dikke", "wit → witte, snel → snelle"],
   ["f becomes v", "lief → lieve", "doof → dove"],
   ["s becomes z", "grijs → grijze", "boos → boze, but: vies → vieze"],
   ["no -e: adjectives in -en", "open, gesloten", "de open deur, de gouden ring"],
   ["no -e: materials in -en", "houten, wollen", "de houten tafel"]]},
  {"type": "verbpairs", "title": "Common adjectives", "items": [
   ["groot", "big, large"], ["klein", "small"], ["oud", "old"], ["nieuw", "new"], ["jong", "young"],
   ["goed", "good"], ["slecht", "bad"], ["goedkoop", "cheap"], ["duur", "expensive"], ["mooi", "beautiful, nice"],
   ["lelijk", "ugly"], ["makkelijk", "easy"], ["moeilijk", "difficult"], ["warm", "warm, hot"], ["koud", "cold"],
   ["lang", "long, tall"], ["kort", "short"], ["lekker", "tasty, nice"]]},
  {"type": "callout", "kind": "tip", "title": "lekker: one word for a lot", "text": "<b>lekker</b> is used for good food (<i>Het eten is lekker</i>), but also for nice weather, a pleasant feeling or comfort: <i>lekker weer, lekker slapen, Lekker!</i> It is one of the most Dutch words there is."},
  {"type": "h1", "text": "3. Comparing"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "Add <b>-er</b> to compare (<i>groter</i>) and <b>-st</b> for the most (<i>het grootst</i>). Use <b>dan</b> for <i>than</i>: <i>Londen is groter dan Amsterdam.</i> Dutch adds -er even to long words where English uses <i>more</i>: <i>interessanter, moeilijker</i>. The -e rules still apply: <i>een grotere stad, de grootste stad</i>."},
  {"type": "table", "style": "plain", "widths": [4.4, 4.4, 4.4, 3.8], "head": ["Adjective", "Comparative", "Superlative", "English"], "rows": [
   ["groot", "groter", "het grootst", "big"],
   ["duur", "duurder", "het duurst", "expensive (after r: -der)"],
   ["moeilijk", "moeilijker", "het moeilijkst", "difficult"],
   ["goed", "beter", "het best", "good, better, best"],
   ["veel", "meer", "het meest", "much, more, most"],
   ["graag", "liever", "het liefst", "gladly: like, prefer"]]},
  {"type": "h1", "text": "4. Common mistakes"},
  {"type": "mistakes", "rows": [
   ["een grote huis", "een groot huis", "een + het-word: no -e."],
   ["de groot stad", "de grote stad", "After de: -e."],
   ["Het huis is grote.", "Het huis is groot.", "After the verb: never -e."],
   ["de dike man", "de dikke man", "Short vowel: double consonant."],
   ["de liefe hond", "de lieve hond", "f becomes v."],
   ["Hij is meer groot dan ik.", "Hij is groter dan ik.", "Comparative: -er."],
   ["groter als", "groter dan", "Than is dan."]]},
  {"type": "h1", "text": "5. Self-check"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "Fill in the right form of the adjective. The answers are on the last page."},
  {"type": "exercises", "items": [
   {"q": "Wij wonen in een ______ huis.", "hint": "groot", "a": "groot", "full": "Wij wonen in een groot huis."},
   {"q": "Het ______ huis is van mijn oom.", "hint": "groot", "a": "grote", "full": "Het grote huis is van mijn oom."},
   {"q": "Ik heb een ______ fiets.", "hint": "nieuw, de fiets", "a": "nieuwe", "full": "Ik heb een nieuwe fiets."},
   {"q": "Mijn koffie is ______.", "hint": "koud", "a": "koud", "full": "Mijn koffie is koud."},
   {"q": "Hij draagt een ______ jas.", "hint": "wit, de jas", "a": "witte", "full": "Hij draagt een witte jas."},
   {"q": "Wat een ______ hond!", "hint": "lief, de hond", "a": "lieve", "full": "Wat een lieve hond!"},
   {"q": "Dit is een ______ boek.", "hint": "goed, het boek", "a": "goed", "full": "Dit is een goed boek."},
   {"q": "Londen is ______ dan Amsterdam.", "hint": "groot, comparative", "a": "groter", "full": "Londen is groter dan Amsterdam."},
   {"q": "Dit is de ______ stad van Nederland.", "hint": "oud, superlative", "a": "oudste", "full": "Dit is de oudste stad van Nederland."},
   {"q": "Thee vind ik ______ dan koffie.", "hint": "lekker, comparative", "a": "lekkerder", "full": "Thee vind ik lekkerder dan koffie."},
   {"q": "Ik drink ______ thee dan koffie.", "hint": "graag, comparative", "a": "liever", "full": "Ik drink liever thee dan koffie."},
   {"q": "Het is een ______ vraag.", "hint": "moeilijk, de vraag", "a": "moeilijke", "full": "Het is een moeilijke vraag."}]},
  {"type": "p", "text": "<b>Translate into Dutch:</b>"},
  {"type": "translations", "items": [
   {"q": "We live in a big house.", "a": "We wonen in een groot huis."},
   {"q": "The new car is expensive.", "a": "De nieuwe auto is duur."},
   {"q": "London is bigger than Amsterdam.", "a": "Londen is groter dan Amsterdam."},
   {"q": "I prefer tea.", "a": "Ik drink liever thee."}]},
  {"type": "pagebreak"},
  {"type": "answers"}
 ]
}
